    {"id":"t2p-1-1","moduleId":"topik2_passages","type":"sentence","target":"한국은 봄, 여름, 가을, 겨울의 사계절이 있습니다.","translation":"Korea has four seasons: spring, summer, autumn, and winter."},
    {"id":"t2p-1-2","moduleId":"topik2_passages","type":"sentence","target":"봄에는 예쁜 꽃이 피고 날씨가 따뜻합니다.","translation":"In spring, pretty flowers bloom and the weather is warm."},
    {"id":"t2p-2-1","moduleId":"topik2_passages","type":"sentence","target":"한글은 세종대왕이 1443년에 만든 한국의 문자입니다.","translation":"Hangeul is the Korean alphabet created by King Sejong in 1443."},
    {"id":"t2p-2-2","moduleId":"topik2_passages","type":"sentence","target":"한글은 배우기 쉽고 과학적인 글자입니다.","translation":"Hangeul is easy to learn and scientific."},
    {"id":"t2p-3-1","moduleId":"topik2_passages","type":"sentence","target":"지난 주말에 친구와 함께 제주도로 여행을 갔습니다.","translation":"Last weekend I went on a trip to Jeju Island with my friend."},
    {"id":"t2p-3-2","moduleId":"topik2_passages","type":"sentence","target":"제주도의 푸른 바다가 참 아름다웠습니다.","translation":"Jeju Island's blue sea was very beautiful."},
    {"id":"t2p-4-1","moduleId":"topik2_passages","type":"sentence","target":"저는 아침 일곱 시에 일어나서 운동을 합니다.","translation":"I wake up at seven in the morning and exercise."},
    {"id":"t2p-4-2","moduleId":"topik2_passages","type":"sentence","target":"아침을 먹고 지하철을 타고 회사에 갑니다.","translation":"After eating breakfast, I take the subway to work."},
    {"id":"t2p-5","moduleId":"topik2_passages","type":"sentence","target":"정직한 나무꾼이 산에서 나무를 하다가, 실수로 쇠도끼를 호수에 빠뜨렸습니다.","translation":"An honest woodcutter accidentally dropped his iron axe into a lake while chopping wood in the mountains."},
    {"id":"t2p-6","moduleId":"topik2_passages","type":"sentence","target":"옛날 옛날에 흥부하고 놀부라는 형제가 살았습니다.","translation":"Once upon a time, there lived two brothers named Heungbu and Nolbu."},
    {"id":"t2p-7","moduleId":"topik2_passages","type":"sentence","target":"흥부는 마음씨가 착했지만, 놀부는 아주 욕심이 많았습니다.","translation":"Heungbu had a kind heart, but Nolbu was very greedy."},
    {"id":"t2p-8","moduleId":"topik2_passages","type":"sentence","target":"놀부는 흥부 가족을 집에서 쫓아냈습니다.","translation":"Nolbu kicked Heungbu's family out of the house."},
    {"id":"t2p-9","moduleId":"topik2_passages","type":"sentence","target":"흥부 가족은 아주 가난하게 초가집에 살았습니다.","translation":"Heungbu's family lived poorly in a thatched-roof house."},
    {"id":"t2p-10","moduleId":"topik2_passages","type":"sentence","target":"어느 날 흥부는 다리가 부러진 제비를 정성껏 치료해 주었습니다.","translation":"One day, Heungbu carefully treated a swallow that had a broken leg."},
    {"id":"t2p-11","moduleId":"topik2_passages","type":"sentence","target":"제비는 보답으로 흥부에게 박씨를 가져다주었습니다.","translation":"As a reward, the swallow brought a gourd seed to Heungbu."},
    {"id":"t2p-12","moduleId":"topik2_passages","type":"sentence","target":"흥부가 박을 타자 금과 은이 쏟아져 나왔습니다.","translation":"When Heungbu opened the gourd, gold and silver poured out."},
    {"id":"t2p-13","moduleId":"topik2_passages","type":"sentence","target":"욕심꾸러기 놀부는 제비의 다리를 일부러 부러뜨렸습니다.","translation":"The greedy Nolbu intentionally broke the swallow's leg."},
    {"id":"t2p-14","moduleId":"topik2_passages","type":"sentence","target":"놀부의 박에서는 도깨비들이 나와 재산을 다 빼앗았습니다.","pronunciation":"nolbuui bageseon dokkaebideuri nawa jaesaneul da ppaeasatseumnida.","translation":"Goblins came out of Nolbu's gourd and took all his wealth."},
    {"id":"t2p-16-1","moduleId":"topik2_passages","type":"sentence","target":"옛날에 아주 배고픈 오누이가 살았습니다.","translation":"Once upon a time, there lived very hungry siblings."},
    {"id":"t2p-16-2","moduleId":"topik2_passages","type":"sentence","target":"오누이는 떡을 가지고 길을 가고 있었습니다.","translation":"The siblings were walking on the road with rice cakes."},
    {"id":"t2p-17","moduleId":"topik2_passages","type":"sentence","target":"그때 무서운 호랑이가 나타나 \"떡 하나 주면 안 잡아먹겠다!\"라고 말했습니다.","pronunciation":"geuttae museoun horangiga natana \"tteok hana jumyeon an jabameokgetda!\" rago malhaetseumnida.","translation":"At that time, a scary tiger appeared and said, \"Give me a rice cake, and I won't eat you!\""},
    {"id":"t2p-18-1","moduleId":"topik2_passages","type":"sentence","target":"오누이는 하늘에 올라가기 위해 하늘에 기도를 했습니다.","translation":"The siblings prayed to the heavens to ascend to the sky."},
    {"id":"t2p-18-2","moduleId":"topik2_passages","type":"sentence","target":"하늘에서 튼튼한 밧줄이 내려왔고, 오누이는 하늘로 올라가 해와 달이 되었습니다.","translation":"A sturdy rope descended from the sky, and the siblings ascended to become the sun and the moon."},
    {"id":"t2p-19-1","moduleId":"topik2_passages","type":"sentence","target":"심청이는 눈먼 아버지를 위해 용기 있는 결정을 했습니다.","translation":"Shim Cheong made a brave decision for her blind father."},
    {"id":"t2p-19-2","moduleId":"topik2_passages","type":"sentence","target":"그녀는 아버지의 눈을 뜨게 하려고 인당수에 제물로 몸을 던졌습니다.","translation":"To restore her father's sight, she threw herself into the Indangsu Sea as a sacrifice."},
    {"id":"t2p-20-1","moduleId":"topik2_passages","type":"sentence","target":"심청이의 효심에 감동한 용왕님은 심청이를 다시 살려주었습니다.","translation":"Moved by Shim Cheong's filial piety, the Dragon King brought her back to life."},
    {"id":"t2p-20-2","moduleId":"topik2_passages","type":"sentence","target":"결국 심청이의 아버지는 눈을 뜨게 되었고, 모두가 행복하게 살았습니다.","translation":"In the end, Shim Cheong's father regained his sight, and everyone lived happily."},
    {"id":"t2p-21-1","moduleId":"topik2_passages","type":"sentence","target":"용왕님이 큰 병에 걸려 몹시 아팠습니다.","translation":"The Dragon King fell very ill and was in great pain."},
    {"id":"t2p-21-2","moduleId":"topik2_passages","type":"sentence","target":"의사는 토끼의 간을 먹어야 병이 나을 것이라고 했습니다.","translation":"The doctor said he would only recover if he ate a rabbit's liver."},
    {"id":"t2p-22-1","moduleId":"topik2_passages","type":"sentence","target":"거북이는 토끼를 잡기 위해 육지로 나갔습니다.","translation":"The turtle went onto land to catch a rabbit."},
    {"id":"t2p-22-2","moduleId":"topik2_passages","type":"sentence","target":"바다를 헤엄쳐 나와 육지의 숲을 찾았습니다.","translation":"He swam out of the sea and searched the forests on land."},
    {"id":"t2p-23-1","moduleId":"topik2_passages","type":"sentence","target":"거북이는 한 나무 아래에서 토끼를 만났습니다.","translation":"The turtle met the rabbit under a tree."},
    {"id":"t2p-23-2","moduleId":"topik2_passages","type":"sentence","target":"거북이는 토끼에게 용궁에 같이 가자고 말했습니다.","translation":"The turtle told the rabbit, \"Let's go to the Dragon Palace together.\""},
    {"id":"t2p-24-1","moduleId":"topik2_passages","type":"sentence","target":"용궁에 도착한 토끼는 깜짝 놀랐습니다.","translation":"The rabbit was shocked when he arrived at the Dragon Palace."},
    {"id":"t2p-24-2","moduleId":"topik2_passages","type":"sentence","target":"용왕님이 토끼의 간을 먹으려고 했기 때문입니다.","translation":"This was because the Dragon King intended to eat his liver."},
    {"id":"t2p-25-1","moduleId":"topik2_passages","type":"sentence","target":"토끼는 재치 있게 \"제 간은 육지에 두고 왔어요\"라고 말했습니다.","translation":"The rabbit cleverly said, \"I left my liver back on land.\""},
    {"id":"t2p-25-2","moduleId":"topik2_passages","type":"sentence","target":"거북이는 토끼의 말을 믿고 다시 육지로 향했습니다.","translation":"The turtle believed the rabbit's words and headed back toward the land."},
    {"id":"t2p-26-1","moduleId":"topik2_passages","type":"sentence","target":"육지에 도착한 토끼는 아주 빠르게 도망쳤습니다.","translation":"Once on land, the rabbit ran away very quickly."},
    {"id":"t2p-26-2","moduleId":"topik2_passages","type":"sentence","target":"토끼는 무사히 숲으로 돌아갔습니다.","translation":"The rabbit safely returned to the forest."}
  ]
}
